IMPORT prelude

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2012 (SA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts in days ("within 14 days after the day", ss 224(3), 226(1), 229(2)), in months ("at
-- least 6 months, but no more than 24 months after", "within 12 months after", s 231(1b); "within 3 months after",
-- "at least every 3 months", s 231(2), (2a); "within 1 month of", s 231(3)(b), (4); "within 1 month after", ss 232(1)(ba),
-- 260A(2); "within 6 months after", s 232(1)(c)), in years ("not more than 1 year after the date", s 113(1); "within 2
-- years after", s 232(1)(a); "for at least 5 years from the day", s 38(7)) and in hours ("within 48 hours", ss 36(c),
-- 38(4)(b); "at least 24 hours after", s 102B(1)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of South
-- Australia, CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Work Health and Safety Act 2012 (SA)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day n days after a day ("within 14 days after the day": the day itself excluded, so the last day is day + 14).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is after` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month n months later (n from 0 to 35); a day the later month does not have falls on that month's
-- last day (31 August + 6 months = 28 or 29 February). Fork F1 in NOTES.md.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`)) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the start` PLUS n
        `the years carried` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 24
            THEN 2
            ELSE IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
                 THEN 1
                 ELSE 0
        `the target month` MEANS `the month count` MINUS (`the years carried` TIMES 12)
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `the years carried`

-- The same day and month n years later; 29 February falls on 28 February in a year that has none (fork F1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` n `years after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the target year`)) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS n
